# Gasoline price update every 5 minutes — install with `crontab -e`
# (or drop into /etc/cron.d/ with a user field: `*/5 * * * * root set -a; ...`).
#
# Cron starts with an empty environment, so source the env file first; `set -a`
# exports every KEY=value it defines (TANKER_KOENIG_API_KEY, storage settings).
# See examples/systemd/gasoline.env for the file this expects at /etc/gasoline/gasoline.env.
#
# `flock -n` keeps the runs from overlapping: cron fires on a fixed schedule
# whether the last run finished or not, and two sweeps at once would race each
# other for the API rate limit and for the database write lock. A radius over
# 25 km is collected as several paced requests and can take a minute or more, so
# the lock is what keeps that safe on a 5-minute schedule.

*/5 * * * * set -a; . /etc/gasoline/gasoline.env; set +a; flock -n /tmp/gasoline-update.lock /usr/local/bin/gasoline update --radius 25 --city 'Luebbecke'
